{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The results of the hair colour of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> people are shown in this circle graph. How many people have blonde hair?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/6780e6031b9b7f36cf3e15e99984502a583e65ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 160 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 180 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 200 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"414\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total percentage should add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, so the total percentage of individuals with blonde hair can be found by finding the total percentage of people with other hair colors, and subtracting the total from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a2c6972a72777c619aa95835700749c5b25f00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - (32\\% + 22\\% + 16\\%) = 30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"283\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> individuals shown in the results had blonde hair, which means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/06050a9d753903a99b897dfd4ab78d341cb66d17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\% \\times 600 = 600 \\times \\frac{30}{100} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C)} 180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"281\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the total number of people that have each hair color, outside of blonde hair. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743bb13121a4d70716f171cae26b000003bdae58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32\\% \\times 600 + 32\\% \\times 600 + 16\\% \\times 600 = 32 \\times 6 + 32 \\times 6 + 16 \\times 6 = 420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"563\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>To find the number of blonde hair individuals, we can then subtract this from the total number of people. We then get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb1b12bd101060d204d0e7e38357f5959bd1ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600 - 420 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl